meta {
  name: Login via CPF (Serverless)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{gatewayUrl}}/auth
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "cpf": "{{clientCpf}}"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.getStatus() === 200 && res.getBody() && res.getBody().token) {
    bru.setEnvVar("clientToken", res.getBody().token);
  }
}

docs {
  Authenticates a workshop client by CPF against the AWS API Gateway.

  The request hits the serverless CPF auth function (os-management-lambda), which:
  1. validates the CPF check digits;
  2. looks the client up in the database and checks it is active;
  3. returns a signed JWT (sub = CPF, roles = ["CLIENT"]).

  The token is stored in the `clientToken` environment variable and is used by the
  "My Orders" / "Decide Order" requests. Point `gatewayUrl` at the `auth_endpoint`
  output of the os-management-gateway Terraform stack (without the trailing /auth).

  Staff (ADMIN / TECHNICIAN) still authenticate with "01 - Login" straight against
  the backend `baseUrl`.
}
